1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,810
Ava: Suppose you're moving a new model from pretraining into agentic RL, then scaling it across hundreds of GPUs.
Ava：假设你要把一个新模型从预训练推进到智能体强化学习，再扩展到数百块 GPU。

2
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:13,017
A small mismatch in model code or numerics can make debugging difficult.
模型代码或数值计算稍有不一致，调试就会变得困难。

3
00:00:13,017 --> 00:00:16,838
That's why this TorchTitan update caught my eye.
所以这次 TorchTitan 更新引起了我的注意。

4
00:00:16,838 --> 00:00:24,184
Brian: TorchTitan is a PyTorch-native platform for experimenting with and training generative models at scale.
Brian：TorchTitan 是一个基于原生 PyTorch 的平台，用于大规模试验和训练生成式模型。

5
00:00:24,184 --> 00:00:34,804
This update keeps its small, extensible design while adding model support, reinforcement learning, performance work, and communication features.
这次更新延续了它小巧、可扩展的设计，同时增加了模型支持、强化学习、性能优化和通信功能。

6
00:00:34,804 --> 00:00:43,483
Ava: The model list is striking: Qwen3.5, Qwen3-VL, Kimi K3, and DeepSeek-V4 are among the additions.
Ava：新增模型名单很亮眼，包括 Qwen3.5、Qwen3-VL、Kimi K3 和 DeepSeek-V4。

7
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:51,066
Are these just model definitions, or can the training stack actually scale them?
这些只是模型定义，还是整个训练系统真能支持它们扩展规模？

8
00:00:51,066 --> 00:00:57,072
Brian: They're full training-stack integrations across TorchTitan's 5D parallelism stack.
Brian：它们都完整接入了 TorchTitan 的 5D 并行训练体系。

9
00:00:57,072 --> 00:01:04,764
The team also introduced typed Python recipes, model-config transforms, and targeted component overrides.
团队还引入了带类型标注的 Python 训练配置、模型配置转换和定向组件覆盖。

10
00:01:04,764 --> 00:01:11,120
Those let users change a training setup without maintaining a separate model fork.
这样用户就能调整训练设置，无须单独维护一个模型分支。

11
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:17,898
Ava: So if a hardware change calls for another parallelization strategy, the recipe can express it.
Ava：所以硬件变化需要另一种并行策略时，可以在训练配置里表达。

12
00:01:17,898 --> 00:01:23,884
If a model needs a different component or kernel, an override can target that part.
如果模型需要替换某个组件或内核，也可以只覆盖那一部分。

13
00:01:23,884 --> 00:01:27,118
The model implementation stays reusable.
模型实现仍可复用。

14
00:01:27,118 --> 00:01:27,774
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

15
00:01:27,774 --> 00:01:39,012
The interfaces also accept optimized Attention Gym kernels, including Gated DeltaNet, Kimi Delta Attention, and sparse-attention kernels.
这些接口也支持经过优化的 Attention Gym 内核，包括 Gated DeltaNet、Kimi Delta Attention 和稀疏注意力内核。

16
00:01:39,012 --> 00:01:42,375
Opt-in Helion kernels include fused RoPE.
可按需启用的 Helion 内核包括融合 RoPE。

17
00:01:42,375 --> 00:01:46,908
These choices remain compatible with torch.compile.
这些选择都与 torch.compile 兼容。

18
00:01:46,908 --> 00:01:52,996
Ava: That raises a question: beyond the model code, what carries over to the next architecture?
Ava：这就引出一个问题：除了模型代码，还有什么能沿用到下一个架构？

19
00:01:52,996 --> 00:02:01,802
A team bringing in a multimodal model would still need data handling, checkpoints, sharding, and a way to check the numerics.
团队引入多模态模型时，仍需要处理数据、检查点、分片，以及验证数值计算。

20
00:02:01,802 --> 00:02:14,483
Brian: The reusable pieces include multimodal data pipelines, sample packing, shared vision components, Hugging Face checkpoint interoperability, declarative sharding, and numerical validation.
Brian：可复用的部分包括多模态数据流水线、样本打包、共享视觉组件、与 Hugging Face 检查点互通、声明式分片和数值验证。

21
00:02:14,483 --> 00:02:20,560
The aim is to make a new architecture ready for validated, scalable training sooner.
目标是让新架构更快具备经过验证的大规模训练能力。

22
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,642
Ava: Now take that model into RL.
Ava：现在把这个模型用于强化学习。

23
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:27,774
Some stacks maintain separate training and inference implementations.
有些系统分别维护训练和推理实现。

24
00:02:27,774 --> 00:02:38,238
An architecture change has to land in both places, and a reward shift becomes hard to diagnose if those implementations quietly diverge.
架构变更得在两处落实；如果两套实现悄悄出现差异，奖励变化就很难排查。

25
00:02:38,238 --> 00:02:45,881
Brian: TitanRL addresses that by keeping the same model from pretraining through post-training and inside vLLM.
Brian：TitanRL 让同一个模型贯穿预训练、后训练，并在 vLLM 中使用，以解决这个问题。

26
00:02:45,881 --> 00:02:47,719
You work in one codebase.
整个过程只需一个代码库。

27
00:02:47,719 --> 00:02:53,948
That doesn't settle every RL question, but it removes one source of model drift.
这不能解决强化学习的所有问题，但能消除一种模型偏移来源。

28
00:02:53,948 --> 00:03:01,925
Ava: Agentic workloads add another pressure point: generation can take time while training needs fresh rollouts.
Ava：智能体任务还有一个压力点：生成可能耗时很久，而训练需要新的采样轨迹。

29
00:03:01,925 --> 00:03:11,146
TitanRL runs rollouts asynchronously, and both generation and training can scale through multiple forms of parallelism.
TitanRL 异步运行采样，生成和训练也都能通过多种并行方式扩展规模。

30
00:03:11,146 --> 00:03:18,878
Brian: The team reports stable training for hundreds of steps on dense and MoE models.
Brian：团队报告称，稠密模型和 MoE 模型都能稳定训练数百步。

31
00:03:18,878 --> 00:03:28,176
The tested tasks include long context, code execution, compaction, harness work, and self-play.
测试任务包括长上下文、代码执行、上下文压缩、测试框架任务和自我对弈。

32
00:03:28,176 --> 00:03:36,552
The figure captions identify Qwen3.5-35B-A3B base runs with 64K and 128K contexts.
图注标明，Qwen3.5-35B-A3B 基础模型的运行使用了 64K 和 128K 上下文。

33
00:03:36,552 --> 00:03:41,653
Ava: Let's make that concrete. Suppose rewards change after you enable a kernel.
Ava：举个具体例子。假设启用一个内核后，奖励发生了变化。

34
00:03:41,653 --> 00:03:49,543
You'd want to know whether the trainer and generator assign the same log probabilities before blaming the algorithm.
在归咎于算法之前，你会想确认训练器和生成器给出的对数概率是否一致。

35
00:03:49,543 --> 00:03:52,070
Can TitanRL check that directly?
TitanRL 能直接检查吗？

36
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:59,869
Brian: In supported on-policy configurations, batch-invariant mode makes their log probabilities bitwise identical.
Brian：在受支持的同策略配置中，批次不变模式能让两者的对数概率逐位一致。

37
00:03:59,869 --> 00:04:02,613
The gap is exactly zero at every step.
每一步的差值都恰好为零。

38
00:04:02,613 --> 00:04:08,740
That gives you a precise check on this part of the training and generation path.
这为训练和生成流程的这一部分提供了精确的检查依据。

39
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,668
Ava: That changes the diagnosis.
Ava：这会改变排查方向。

40
00:04:10,668 --> 00:04:18,239
If the log probabilities match under that mode, you can focus on other possible causes of a reward change.
如果在该模式下对数概率一致，就可以把注意力转向奖励变化的其他可能原因。

41
00:04:18,239 --> 00:04:26,874
The guarantee is specific to supported on-policy configurations; it doesn't promise identical rewards for every run.
这项保证仅适用于受支持的同策略配置，并不保证每次运行的奖励都相同。

42
00:04:26,874 --> 00:04:32,395
Brian: And once a run is behaving correctly, where would you look if it's still slow?
Brian：确认运行正确后，如果速度仍然慢，该从哪里查起？

43
00:04:32,395 --> 00:04:42,512
TorchTitan's performance work groups the problem into faster kernels, more communication and compute overlap, and finer control of memory.
TorchTitan 的性能优化主要围绕更快的内核、更多通信与计算重叠，以及更精细的内存控制。

44
00:04:42,512 --> 00:04:45,363
Ava: One interesting choice is local_compile.
Ava：一个有意思的选择是 local_compile。

45
00:04:45,363 --> 00:04:53,703
It applies native torch.compile selectively to important regions, without requiring full-graph or full-block tracing.
它有选择地对关键区域应用原生 torch.compile，无须追踪整个计算图或整个模块。

46
00:04:53,703 --> 00:05:01,822
That sounds useful when a small part of a model deserves optimization, but you want to preserve its numerics.
如果模型只有一小部分需要优化，而你又想保持数值计算结果，这听起来很有用。

47
00:05:01,822 --> 00:05:08,734
Brian: For memory, torch_remat gives fine-grained control over which activation regions get recomputed.
Brian：在内存方面，torch_remat 可以精细控制哪些激活值区域需要重新计算。

48
00:05:08,734 --> 00:05:18,300
It's an activation checkpointing API that avoids the CPU overhead and custom operator wrappers described for earlier approaches.
它是一个激活值检查点 API，避免了早期方案所述的 CPU 开销和自定义算子封装。

49
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:22,811
Ava: Recomputation trades extra work for less stored activation data.
Ava：重新计算会增加计算量，但能减少需要保存的激活值数据。

50
00:05:22,811 --> 00:05:29,788
The control matters because the best region to recompute can depend on the model and memory budget.
这种控制很重要，因为最适合重新计算的区域取决于模型和内存预算。

51
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:34,226
What does the update do for distributed MoE communication?
这次更新如何改进分布式 MoE 通信？

52
00:05:34,226 --> 00:05:40,227
Brian: Dist-MoE fuses communication with expert compute on NVIDIA SM100+ GPUs.
Brian：Dist-MoE 在 NVIDIA SM100+ GPU 上融合通信与专家计算。

53
00:05:40,227 --> 00:05:47,411
It also packs activations for dynamic tensors so execution can remain CUDA-graphable.
它还为动态张量打包激活值，使执行过程仍可纳入 CUDA 图。

54
00:05:47,411 --> 00:05:56,128
The idea is to overlap token movement and computation rather than treating them as separate stages.
核心思路是让 token 传输与计算重叠执行。

55
00:05:56,128 --> 00:05:59,201
Ava: Pipeline parallelism got a rewrite too.
Ava：流水线并行也经过了重写。

56
00:05:59,201 --> 00:06:07,002
It offers deterministic, CUDA-graphable execution and controls for overlap when combined with FSDP.
它提供确定性的 CUDA 图执行，并支持与 FSDP 结合时控制任务重叠。

57
00:06:07,002 --> 00:06:15,390
That gives users another place to tune the schedule instead of relying on one fixed execution pattern.
用户因此可以进一步调整调度方式。

58
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:24,182
Brian: And TorchTitan overrides can bring in specialized model kernels, such as fused MLA, fused SwiGLU, and fused Complex RoPE.
Brian：TorchTitan 的覆盖机制还能引入专用模型内核，如融合版 MLA、SwiGLU 和 Complex RoPE。

59
00:06:24,182 --> 00:06:34,196
The configuration and override system is what lets those optimizations fit without spreading model-specific code through the trainer.
配置和覆盖系统让这些优化得以接入，而不必在训练器各处加入特定模型的代码。

60
00:06:34,196 --> 00:06:36,601
Ava: Let's put numbers on it.
Ava：来看具体数据。

61
00:06:36,601 --> 00:06:51,433
For DeepSeek V3 671B with its MTP1 module, the team evaluated performance on the MLPerf training benchmark on an internal GB300 cluster using MXFP8.
团队使用 MXFP8，在内部 GB300 集群上，以 MLPerf 训练基准评估了带 MTP1 模块的 DeepSeek V3 671B。

62
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:56,794
The report says it scaled the PP, DP, and EP axes.
报告称测试扩展了 PP、DP 和 EP 三个并行维度。

63
00:06:56,794 --> 00:07:14,866
Brian: With PP at 2, the 256-GPU run reports 5,324.21 tokens per second per GPU and 1,362,998 globally.
Brian：PP 为 2 时，256 块 GPU 的测试结果是每块 GPU 每秒 5,324.21 个 token，全局每秒 1,362,998 个。

64
00:07:14,866 --> 00:07:27,264
At 512 GPUs, it reports 5,262.68 per GPU and 2,694,493 globally.
512 块 GPU 时，分别为每块 GPU 每秒 5,262.68 个、全局每秒 2,694,493 个。

65
00:07:27,264 --> 00:07:33,628
Ava: Here's the catch: the local batch size and microbatch count also change between those runs.
Ava：但要注意，这两次测试的本地批大小和微批次数也不同。

66
00:07:33,628 --> 00:07:43,838
The higher global throughput is real for the reported configurations, but those numbers alone don't establish a fixed-workload scaling curve.
所报告配置的全局吞吐量确实更高，但仅凭这些数字无法得出固定工作负载下的扩展曲线。

67
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:50,730
Brian: The Muse Spark Open table shows why configuration details matter.
Brian：Muse Spark Open 的数据表说明了配置细节为何重要。

68
00:07:50,730 --> 00:08:02,075
On the same setup, at 256 GPUs and 96K context, learned routing reports 1,500.61 tokens per second per GPU.
在相同环境下，256 块 GPU、96K 上下文时，学习式路由达到每块 GPU 每秒 1,500.61 个 token。

69
00:08:02,075 --> 00:08:06,772
Forced balanced routing reports 1,839.52.
强制均衡路由达到 1,839.52 个。

70
00:08:06,772 --> 00:08:13,588
Ava: And the table also has 512-GPU runs at 192K context, with more context parallelism.
Ava：表中还有 512 块 GPU、192K 上下文的测试，采用了更多上下文并行。

71
00:08:13,588 --> 00:08:21,389
I'd keep the routing choice, context length, and parallelism visible when comparing those rows.
比较这些数据时，我会明确标出路由方式、上下文长度和并行配置。

72
00:08:21,389 --> 00:08:26,994
A single throughput figure would hide useful engineering detail.
只看单个吞吐量数字会掩盖有用的工程细节。

73
00:08:26,994 --> 00:08:31,954
Brian: TorchTitan is also showing up outside its own training recipes.
Brian：TorchTitan 也开始用于自身训练方案之外。

74
00:08:31,954 --> 00:08:44,192
The update names veRL and Miles as integrations, says it's Meshy's default training backend, and says it inspires Archon, the training engine in Areal.
更新提到它已与 veRL 和 Miles 集成，是 Meshy 的默认训练后端，并启发了 Areal 中的训练引擎 Archon。

75
00:08:44,192 --> 00:08:51,191
Ava: Another scaling issue sits below the model: how parameters and optimizer state are sharded.
Ava：另一个扩展问题在模型底层：参数和优化器状态如何切分。

76
00:08:51,191 --> 00:09:01,805
FSDP2 supports row-wise and column-wise sharding, but distributed Muon and blockwise parameter quantization benefit from other placements.
FSDP2 支持按行和按列切分，但分布式 Muon 和分块参数量化适合其他放置方式。

77
00:09:01,805 --> 00:09:04,462
That's where FlexShard enters.
这正是 FlexShard 的用武之地。

78
00:09:04,462 --> 00:09:07,700
Brian: FlexShard works with buckets of parameters.
Brian：FlexShard 按参数桶工作。

79
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:15,229
Each bucket gets a Placement policy, and its runtime overlaps bucket communication with computation.
每个桶都有一个 Placement 策略，运行时会让桶通信与计算重叠。

80
00:09:15,229 --> 00:09:18,316
Owned gives one rank an entire parameter.
Owned 让一个 rank 持有完整参数。

81
00:09:18,316 --> 00:09:24,012
BlockShard uses two-dimensional tiles aligned with the sharding scheme.
BlockShard 使用与切分方案对齐的二维分块。

82
00:09:24,012 --> 00:09:32,349
Ava: For distributed Muon, those placements avoid All Gather before the optimizer update.
Ava：对于分布式 Muon，这些放置方式避免了优化器更新前的 All Gather。

83
00:09:32,349 --> 00:09:45,602
On DeepSeek V3 at 256 H100 GPUs, the reported optimizer time improves by up to 79% against an equivalent FSDP-only implementation.
在 256 块 H100 GPU 上运行 DeepSeek V3 时，报告称优化器耗时相比等效的纯 FSDP 实现最多缩短 79%。

84
00:09:45,602 --> 00:09:51,260
Brian: BlockShard also aligns sharding with blockwise quantization.
Brian：BlockShard 还使切分方式与分块量化对齐。

85
00:09:51,260 --> 00:10:00,030
It allows FP8-quantized parameter AllGathers without extra communication for scaling factors.
这样就能对 FP8 量化参数执行 AllGather，且无需为缩放因子增加通信。

86
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:10,120
Gathering parameters in FP8 reduces communication volume by about 50% compared with gathering them in BF16.
相比汇集 BF16 参数，汇集 FP8 参数可减少约 50% 的通信量。

87
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:16,600
On Llama3 405B at 256 H100 GPUs, step time improves by up to 20%.
在 256 块 H100 GPU 上运行 Llama3 405B 时，单步耗时最多缩短 20%。

88
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:21,809
Ava: GraphTrainer takes a different route: it builds an explicit training graph.
Ava：GraphTrainer 采用另一种方式：构建显式训练图。

89
00:10:21,809 --> 00:10:28,547
TorchTitan says its graph-based and eager-based paths produce bitwise-matching numerical results.
TorchTitan 表示，图模式与即时执行模式的数值结果逐位一致。

90
00:10:28,547 --> 00:10:35,982
The graph path can support cross-module fusions, graph-level debugging, and tailored hardware support.
图模式可支持跨模块融合、图级调试和定制硬件支持。

91
00:10:35,982 --> 00:10:39,775
Brian: Communication infrastructure changed as well.
Brian：通信基础设施也有变化。

92
00:10:39,775 --> 00:10:46,265
In PyTorch 2.14, an opt-in NCCL backend from torchcomms was ported into c10d.
在 PyTorch 2.14 中，torchcomms 的一个可选 NCCL 后端被移植到 c10d。

93
00:10:46,265 --> 00:10:57,740
It registers under the usual nccl name and adds features including one-sided RMA windows and in-place process-group reconfiguration.
它沿用常见的 nccl 名称注册，并增加了单边 RMA 窗口、进程组原地重新配置等功能。

94
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:02,584
Ava: Symmetric memory connects that infrastructure to training.
Ava：对称内存把这些基础设施与训练连接起来。

95
00:11:02,584 --> 00:11:10,352
Dist-MoE moves tokens between experts through it and fuses that movement with expert compute.
Dist-MoE 通过对称内存在专家之间传输 token，并将传输与专家计算融合。

96
00:11:10,352 --> 00:11:18,970
TorchTitan's FSDP can also place communication buffers in a symmetric memory pool for NCCL kernels.
TorchTitan 的 FSDP 还能将 NCCL 内核的通信缓冲区放入对称内存池。

97
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:22,576
Brian: At that scale, checkpoint coordination matters too.
Brian：在这种规模下，检查点的协调也很重要。

98
00:11:22,576 --> 00:11:32,051
The new torch_checkpointing library shares metadata with one collective before the first save and uses a lightweight barrier per save.
新的 torch_checkpointing 库在首次保存前通过一次集合通信共享元数据，此后每次保存使用轻量级同步屏障。

99
00:11:32,051 --> 00:11:37,704
The older GLOO-based synchronization approach scales poorly past 16K ranks.
旧的 GLOO 同步方式在超过 16K 个 rank 后扩展效果较差。

100
00:11:37,704 --> 00:11:58,878
Ava: In the reported 512-H100-GPU DeepSeek V3 671B run with checkpoint interval 50, average trainer blocking time falls from 841.2 ms with DCPv1 to 34.1 ms with torch_checkpointing.
Ava：在报告的 512 块 H100 GPU、检查点间隔为 50 的 DeepSeek V3 671B 测试中，训练器平均阻塞时间从 DCPv1 的 841.2 毫秒降至 torch_checkpointing 的 34.1 毫秒。

101
00:11:58,878 --> 00:12:06,326
Average checkpoint write time falls from 384.4 s to 13.1 s.
检查点平均写入时间从 384.4 秒降至 13.1 秒。

102
00:12:06,326 --> 00:12:12,862
Brian: Average non-resharding load time falls too, from 194.7 s to 79 s in that setup.
Brian：在该配置下，无需重新分片时的平均加载时间也从 194.7 秒降至 79 秒。

103
00:12:12,862 --> 00:12:16,089
Those are substantial measured changes.
这些都是实测的大幅改善。

104
00:12:16,089 --> 00:12:25,540
They also come from a named model, GPU count, and checkpoint configuration, so I'd keep that context attached.
这些数据对应特定的模型、GPU 数量和检查点配置，因此需要连同这些条件一起看。

105
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:41,057
Ava: The useful takeaway for me is how the pieces fit: reusable model integrations, one model path into TitanRL, checks for numerical agreement, and more control over compute, memory, and sharding.
Ava：对我来说，关键是这些部分如何配合：可复用的模型集成、接入 TitanRL 的统一模型路径、数值一致性检查，以及对计算、内存和分片更灵活的控制。

106
00:12:41,057 --> 00:12:51,186
The qualifications matter: batch-invariant mode has supported on-policy configurations, and Dist-MoE targets SM100+ GPUs.
但也要注意适用范围：批次不变模式仅支持部分同策略配置，Dist-MoE 则面向 SM100+ GPU。

107
00:12:51,186 --> 00:12:58,731
Brian: And the performance tables give concrete configurations to study, rather than one universal speed claim.
Brian：性能表也列出了可供研究的具体配置，不能把它们概括成普遍适用的提速幅度。

108
00:12:58,731 --> 00:13:03,374
TorchTitan's team invites feedback as people try these features.
TorchTitan 团队欢迎大家试用这些功能并提供反馈。

109
00:13:03,374 --> 00:13:07,496
That's our look at the update. Thanks for listening.
这次更新就介绍到这里。感谢收听。
